# Example 02: Set Extended VLAN Tagging Op Config Data — Parameter Error (0x03)
#
# Two-frame exchange: OLT sends Set request with a malformed 16-byte VLAN rule tuple,
# ONU responds with result code 0x03.
# Hex is fabricated for illustration; CRC fields are placeholders (00000000).
#
# Baseline frame layout (48 bytes):
#   [0-1]  TCID
#   [2]    Message Type  (AR/AK bits + MT)
#   [3]    Device ID     (0x0A = baseline OMCI)
#   [4-5]  ME Class ID
#   [6-7]  ME Instance ID
#   [8-9]  Attribute Mask (which attributes are being set)
#   [10-39] Attribute values (up to 30 bytes in baseline frame)
#   [40-43] OMCI Trailer (0x0028 + MIC placeholder)
#   [44-47] CRC-32       (placeholder 00000000)
#
# ME 171 — Extended VLAN Tagging Operation Configuration Data
#   ME Class ID: 0x00AB (171)
#   Attribute 7 — "Received frame VLAN tagging operation table" (16-byte rule tuples)
#   Attribute mask bit 7 (from MSB) = 0x0100
#
# Frame 1 — OLT->ONU: Set request (MT=8=0x08, AR=1 -> MessageType byte = 0x48)
#   TCID=0x0002, DevID=0x0A, MEClass=0x00AB (171), MEInst=0x0001
#   AttrMask=0x0100 (attribute 7 only)
#   Rule bytes [12-27]: deliberately malformed — filter outer priority=0xF (reserved),
#     VID=0xFFF (wildcard), TPID=0xEEEE (invalid), treatment outer priority=0xFF (invalid)
#   NOTE: byte offsets are illustrative; actual G.988 encoding may vary by implementation
000248AB00AB000101000FFFEEEEFFFFFFFF0000000000000000000000000000000000280000000000000000
#
# Frame 2 — ONU->OLT: Set response (MT=8=0x08, AK=1 -> MessageType byte = 0x28)
#   TCID=0x0002, DevID=0x0A, MEClass=0x00AB (171), MEInst=0x0001
#   Content byte 0 = 0x03 (result code: Parameter Error)
#   Content byte 1 = 0x00 (unsupported attribute mask — unused for this error)
000228AB00AB000103000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000002800000000
